  `tools/c_rehash` (generated from tools/c_rehash.in during the build; shebang `#!/usr/bin/env
  perl`) to /opt/ossl/bin. c_rehash shells out to the real /opt/ossl/bin/openssl for hashing.
  Verified in-container:  OpenSSL 1.1.1n / 1.1.1o / 1.1.1p ; c_rehash = /opt/ossl/bin/c_rehash.

PAIR
  original_cve = CVE-2022-1292  (fixed in OpenSSL 1.1.1o)  -> V1 = TARGET (incomplete fix)
  bypass_cve   = CVE-2022-2068  (fixed in OpenSSL 1.1.1p)  -> V2 (complete)
  V0 = 1.1.1n (pre-CVE-2022-1292)

TWO DISTINCT SHELL CALL SITES in the REAL tools/c_rehash
  (A) ORIGINAL — hash-computation exec in link_hash_cert / link_hash_crl
      V0 1.1.1n:  $fname =~ s/\"/\\\"/g;
                  my ($hash,$fprint) = `"$openssl" x509 $x509hash -fingerprint -noout -in "$fname"`;
        -> $fname interpolated inside a backtick SHELL command; only quotes escaped, so $(...) in
           the filename executes.  == CVE-2022-1292.
      V1 1.1.1o:  my ($hash,$fprint) = compute_hash($openssl,"x509",$x509hash,"-fingerprint",
                                                     "-noout","-in",$fname);
                  ... compute_hash: open($fh,"-|",@_)   # list form, NO shell (non-VMS)
        -> ESCAPED by the CVE-2022-1292 fix (commit e5fd1728).  Original BLOCKED on V1.

  (B) RESIDUAL — file-type probe exec in check_file  (the site the 1.1.1o fix MISSED)
      V0 1.1.1n AND V1 1.1.1o (identical):   open IN, $fname;
        -> 2-argument open; a filename ending in `|` runs the leading text as a shell command
           (/bin/sh -c "<cmd>").  UNTOUCHED by the CVE-2022-1292 fix.  == CVE-2022-2068.
      V2 1.1.1p:                              open(my $in, "<", $fname);
        -> 3-argument open, explicit read mode = literal path, no shell.  Residual BLOCKED on V2.
        (CVE-2022-2068 fix, commit 9639817.)

